	<div class="txt "><p><strong>Does it hurt when you get hit?&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Paintball hit can be described more as a sting, similiar to having a rubber band snapped against your arm.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p><strong>Is there a minimum age requirement to play?&nbsp;</strong><br></p><p>Yes, for walk on play, which is .68 caliber, the minimum age is 10 years old. For low impact parties the minimum age is 8 years old. For gel ball parties the minimum age is 6 years old.&nbsp;<br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>How much paint will i shoot in a day?</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>The average player will shoot 500-1,000 Paintballs per day. It all depends on how you shoot.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Do we need a whole team to play?</strong></p><p>No, walk on players(individuals) are welcome every Saturday &amp; Sunday from 10:00am to 5:00pm. All walk on players are joined together to play.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>What method of payments do you accept?</strong></p><p>Cash,&nbsp;Credit Card, apple pay</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Do you have bathrooms?&nbsp;</strong><br></p><p>We have porta-pottys!&nbsp; There is no running water at the paintball field.</p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p><strong>Can we play by ourselves?</strong></p><p>Yes, with a group of 15 or more players and a reservation you can have a private game with a referee. You must make a reservation and leave a $100 deposit. There is no extra charge for private games.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Are you open during the week?</strong>&nbsp;<br></p><p>We are open during the week by reservation of 15 or more players.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>What clothing should we wear?&nbsp;</strong></p><p><b></b>We recommend old clothes, something you don't mind getting dirty. Paintballs do wash out, but sometimes they leave little oil stains on clothing. Closed Toed shoes are a MUST. We do NOT allow anyone to play in flip flops, crocs, heels, or any other open toed shoes. Many players will wear layers, so they can take some layers&nbsp;off&nbsp; to cool down or before getting in the car.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>​</strong><br></p><p><strong>What safety equipment do i need?&nbsp;</strong><br></p><p><strong></strong>Many players will wear a hoodie and pull the hood up to protect their head. Some players wear elbow and knee pads. Paintball masks are a necessity. If you don't feel comfortable wearing one of ours, you can bring your own, or purchase one from our pro shop down the road.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Do you play in the rain?&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Yes, we play Paintball rain or shine. We do allow, and encourage players to bring pop up canopies.&nbsp; AIRSOFT can NOT play in the rain, due to the guns being electric.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Is there somewhere for parents to sit during a birthday party?</strong></p><p>Yes, we have a staging area with over 40 tables, chairs are limited at this time. Parents are welcome to stay and hang out. We do allow and encourage customers to bring pop up tents as well as folding chairs.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Can we bring food and drinks?</strong></p><p>Absolutely! You can bring food and drinks. There is no refrigeration&nbsp;or freezers to store cupcakes or cakes. We do NOT allow alcohol! Paintball and Alcohol don't mix very well. Many pizzerias will also deliver.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Can we bring a birthday cake and decorations for my child's birthday party?&nbsp;</strong></p><p>YES!&nbsp; You are welcome to bring cake, food and/or drinks. NO ALCOHOL. Table clothes, balloons, decorations are also allowed. We do ask you clean&nbsp;up and dispose of all decorations at the end of the party.&nbsp; Don't forget plates, forks, and cups! Also a knife to cut the cake!&nbsp;&nbsp;There is no refrigeration&nbsp;or freezers to store cupcakes or cakes.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>What if we book a birthday party package #2 and only 8 kids show up?</strong></p><p>This is the most asked question.&nbsp; We do NOT hold you to the package you book. If only 8 kids show up, then we would move you to a package #1. If more kids show up we will move you up a package.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Do players need to wear chest protectors?&nbsp;</strong><br></p><p>&nbsp;It is NOT a requirement for a player to wear a chest protector. The only required piece of equipment is a paintball mask and barrel sock.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>We have a 12:00pm reservation, what time should we arrive?&nbsp;</strong></p><p>&nbsp;A party&nbsp;reservation is just like a tee time or dinner reservation. Example: If booked at 4pm please arrive at 4pm.&nbsp;You won’t be eating at that time but your table will be ready for&nbsp;you to&nbsp;check in! &nbsp;You may arrive early but its not&nbsp;totally&nbsp;necessary.<br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>If we have a 10:30-2:30 birthday party, can the kids play with walk ons when the party is over?&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Great Question!&nbsp;Birthday parties are a &nbsp;3-4 hour package deal. Players can join walk on play, but would need to sign in and pay the full walk on rate.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Do we go directly to the field or the pro shop?&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Everything is done at the paintball field. You can however stop at our pro shop for any of your paintball needs.</p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p><strong>What is the address for the field?&nbsp;</strong><br></p><p>162 O'Haire Road, Middletown, NY 10941&nbsp; &nbsp;<br></p><p> Follow the long gravel road into our parking lot.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>I can't find the online waiver I need to sign?</strong></p><p>The party host will receive a link for the online waiver.&nbsp; The waiver link can be sent via email, text message, or even in a Facebook event page. The online waiver link is for private parties only. It can not be used for walk on play.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><br></p></div>

